<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level5-ic-story-bridge> {
  ex:ic-question a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-question-h, ex:ic-question-c ; cd:narration "Distinguish description from inference. Computing spread tells us what happened in one series, not how unusual it would be under an unchanged method. The sample SD is a random estimate, not the fixed true SD. Our question is how frequently six independent readings under unchanged precision would yield at least this much spread. Keep that question open while comparing new series and building the sampling reference. A distribution name or rescaling alone cannot answer it."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ic-question-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "A larger sample SD is not yet a test decision"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ic-question-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ic-question-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ic-question-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ic-question-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ic-scale-question a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-scale-question-h, ex:ic-scale-question-c ; cd:narration "The missing ingredient was a sampling reference, not a better summary of the same six data. Comparing raw variances directly by simulation is valid. Chi-square supplies a convenient exact normal-model reference after scaling. Multiply sample variance by five residual df and divide by the fixed reference variance. This changes scale and units, not ordering or upper-tail probability. Variance 0.024 and scaled statistic twelve represent the same evidence, not two findings. Use the five independent normal residual directions to justify the reference, rather than treating the six raw residuals as independent. Only after this calibration make the decision."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ic-scale-question-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Why scale the variance if we already know its value"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ic-scale-question-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ic-scale-question-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ic-scale-question-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ic-scale-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
